        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Excuse My French, Pop That\n- People: Machine Gun Kelly, Richard Colson Baker, MGK, Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Raekwon, Scarface, Snoop Dogg\n- Places: Cleveland, Ohio\n- Topics: guest appearances, music career\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Colson Baker, better known as MGK or Machine Gun Kelly, was born on April 22, 1990, and is an American rapper and actor from Cleveland, Ohio.\n- Machine Gun Kelly began his musical career as a teenager and released a mixtape in 2006.\n- The song \"Pop That\" was released as the first single from the 2013 debut studio album \"Excuse My French.\"\n- \"Pop That\" features guest appearances from Rick Ross, Drake, and Lil Wayne.\n- The album \"Excuse My French\" features guest appearances from Diddy, Nicki Minaj, Drake, Ace Hood, Lil Wayne, Birdman, The Weeknd, Rick Ross, 2 Chainz, Max B, Ne-Yo, Machine Gun Kelly, Raekwon, Scarface, and Snoop Dogg, among others.",
